  },
  {
   "@id": "http://localhost:8080/cost-of-moving-to-nyc/#faq",
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Start with the movers' range for your home and route, then add the first month's rent, a security deposit of up to one month's rent, and a broker fee only if you hire your own broker. Movers alone charge $380–$960 for a 1-bedroom moved 10 road miles, off peak, with no stairs or extras. Keep a cushion of a few months' living costs on top, because most of the cost of moving to NYC is paid before your first paycheck."
     },
     "name": "How much money should you save before moving to NYC?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes. The calculator at the top of this page prices the movers' share of the cost of moving to NYC from your ZIP code, for your home size and date. It's free and needs no email. Add the lease's upfront costs to its range for the full figure."
     },
     "name": "Is there a calculator for the cost of moving to NYC?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Only if you hire the broker yourself. Since June 11, 2025, the FARE Act has barred brokers who represent the landlord from charging the tenant. Listings must also disclose any fees a tenant will pay."
     },
     "name": "Do you still pay a broker fee to rent in New York City?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Many New York landlords look for yearly income of about 40 times the monthly rent, or a guarantor who earns about 80 times. If you don't meet that, a guarantor company can back the lease for a fee. Count that fee in the cost of moving to NYC if you are starting a new job in the city."
     },
     "name": "What salary do you need to rent an apartment in NYC?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Long-distance movers usually give a delivery window of several days rather than one fixed date, and a longer haul gets a wider window. Get the window in writing with the estimate. If your lease starts first, plan a few nights on an air mattress or in a short-term rental."
     },
     "name": "How long does a long-distance delivery to NYC take?"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}